{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/996398-anyone-make-exigents-as-playable-characters","id":996398,"title":"Anyone make Exigents as playable Characters?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Exigents"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-31T19:25:33-07:00","id":996398,"title":"Anyone make Exigents as playable Characters?","content":"I'm thinking of having one of my players Exalt as an Exigents/one off Exalt tied to Evocations like Sora or Bleach Style Shinigami. So he can have access to Evocations, two levels of sorcery, and Martial Arts with other charms themed after they style of their artifacts. He doesn't know Exalted and super DnD heavy and likely will be able to play once a month or so. So I figure this may give him some simplified options that allow him to simulate being a &quot;Spellsword&quot; he mentions. <br /> <br /> Right now he along with everyone is still mortals. <br /> <br /> <br /> Exigents with the looses guidelines would be easier to pull of rather then doing something like build up already existing Exalts like Lunars or infernals.<br /> <br /> <br /> Anyone tap into playing Exigents yet?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T07:54:30-07:00","id":996588,"title":"","content":"Not to put down anyone's creative efforts...but I never really got the notion of playing a splat before its rules come out. I was honestly a bit baffled when people where so taken by Liminals that they were posting their Liminal PCs, and this was a couple of years ago! We still know sooo little about the new Exalts, even with the Dev's comments...far less than we knew about the original Exalted when the 1E Core came out, way back then.<br /> <br /> I guess I'm just afraid of a fan backlash when the mechanics are finally printed, and it turns out that the PCs they previously conceived of (and in some cases spent actual years invested in) are actually not possible. So now they have to either ignore the rules and go with their original concepts or play something unlike what they wanted. <br /> <br /> And the earliest we can expect to see any solid data on them is, what, still a year or so away, at least?<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Personally, I'm mostly just ignoring them, until we get some real info on them. I've come up with a few Exigent ideas, but I wouldn't try to play one yet. Having said all this, Exigents are probably the most interesting of the new ones I've heard about so far, so I'm also interested in hearing about people's actual play experiences...and if they will change their PCs when/if the actual book comes out with unexpected mechanics!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T14:22:02-07:00","id":996804,"title":"","content":"I fell in love with the idea of the Exigence Exalted when I first heard about them. While I haven't made a full fledged PC by making up rules for an Exigent, I did post a <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1179-i-m-creating-a-black-market-exigent-for-a-2-5-game\">thread</a> three years ago on this and the old forum for making an Exigent NPC antagonist. I eventually quoted over the responses from the old forum (quoting function went wonky for some reason). Anyway, thanks to the forumites' suggestions, the NPC worked out rather well. Although it's not quite what you asked about, it may be an interesting read or give you some ideas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Good night sweet Green Sun Prince: And flights of demons beat thee to thy rest...with billyclubs! <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/362-darkon","name":"Darkon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar362_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T14:31:30-07:00","id":996813,"title":"","content":"I'd have to echo Hand-of-Omega here. Making an entire splat from scratch is hella hard work (speaking from experience). It'd be vastly easier to make him into a Solar, grab sorcery, and make a lot of evocations based on your weapon. For example, I was trying to make a sword set of evocations based on the DFOG Asura class (Who is a magic swordsman), but was unable to think up other decent charms.<br /> <br /> Oh and balance, as gaining ranged attacks aimed with DEX+Occult in addition to melee abilities is quite strong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T15:09:49-07:00","id":996831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/996398-anyone-make-exigents-as-playable-characters?p=996588#post996588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not to put down anyone's creative efforts...but I never really got the notion of playing a splat before its rules come out. I was honestly a bit baffled when people where so taken by Liminals that they were posting their Liminal PCs, and this was a couple of years ago! We still know sooo little about the new Exalts, even with the Dev's comments...far less than we knew about the original Exalted when the 1E Core came out, way back then.<br /> <br /> I guess I'm just afraid of a fan backlash when the mechanics are finally printed, and it turns out that the PCs they previously conceived of (and in some cases spent actual years invested in) are actually not possible. So now they have to either ignore the rules and go with their original concepts or play something unlike what they wanted.<br /> <br /> And the earliest we can expect to see any solid data on them is, what, still a year or so away, at least?<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Personally, I'm mostly just ignoring them, until we get some real info on them. I've come up with a few Exigent ideas, but I wouldn't try to play one yet. Having said all this, Exigents are probably the most interesting of the new ones I've heard about so far, so I'm also interested in hearing about people's actual play experiences...and if they will change their PCs when/if the actual book comes out with unexpected mechanics!</div> </div> </div> </div>If someone wanted to homebrew a Exigent right now they honestly might not look that different then what a Exigent will look like when the actual book comes out. It all depends on how structured the Exigent book actually ends up being. If the process of creating a Exigent isn't highly structured, more of a free-for-all where you just choose the tiers appropriate to the game, that wouldn't be that different than homebrewing right now. We also don't really know how you will make charms for a Exigent, it could just end up being like evocations in the core book <i>&quot;here are a bunch we have made, now go make your own&quot;</i>, in which case the book might give you a bit more inspiration but won't necessarily provide more help for making them than if you are just working with the core book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5622-sprucestripedgoose","name":"SpruceStripedGoose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5622_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T15:14:50-07:00","id":996836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sandact6</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/996398-anyone-make-exigents-as-playable-characters?p=996813#post996813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd have to echo Hand-of-Omega here. Making an entire splat from scratch is hella hard work (speaking from experience). It'd be vastly easier to make him into a Solar, grab sorcery, and make a lot of evocations based on your weapon. For example, I was trying to make a sword set of evocations based on the DFOG Asura class (Who is a magic swordsman), but was unable to think up other decent charms.<br /> <br /> Oh and balance, as gaining ranged attacks aimed with DEX+Occult in addition to melee abilities is quite strong.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well your not really making an entire splat, and it will still be the same once the Ex book comes out. Really you just need to make the charms the player will want to learn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T16:35:53-07:00","id":996881,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/996398-anyone-make-exigents-as-playable-characters#post996398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm thinking of having one of my players Exalt as an Exigents/one off Exalt tied to Evocations like Sora or Bleach Style Shinigami. So he can have access to Evocations, two levels of sorcery, and Martial Arts with other charms themed after they style of their artifacts. He doesn't know Exalted and super DnD heavy and likely will be able to play once a month or so. So I figure this may give him some simplified options that allow him to simulate being a &quot;Spellsword&quot; he mentions.<br /> <br /> Right now he along with everyone is still mortals.<br /> <br /> <br /> Exigents with the looses guidelines would be easier to pull of rather then doing something like build up already existing Exalts like Lunars or infernals.<br /> <br /> <br /> Anyone tap into playing Exigents yet?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm the GM for my group and we haven't tried hacking into any splats like this yet so I don't have much in the way of practical experience here. Because all the exigents at my table have been NPCs I haven't had to worry about player experience and balance. That being said, I'll give you my two cents.<br /> <br /> The first thing I would want to know first is what splat are the other characters? I assume Solar but I don't know if it's a situation where you've made up rules for other splats that they're using. That would effect the power level we were balancing towards.<br /> <br /> The second thing I would want to know is what's his planned play style going to be? Is he going to have a single sword/weapon that he's going to call many evocations from? Or is he going to demonstrate his proficiency at evocations by calling out evocations from lots of different artifacts that he his going to use interchangeably? That might effect what sorts of charms you draw up for him.<br /> <br /> As it stands I have a couple of <b>very rough</b> ideas for charms he can buy:<br /> <br /> 1) Switch weapon as a reflexive action.<br /> 2) Switch armor as a reflexive action.<br /> 3) Evocation Slot (Type: Simple; Duration: Indefinite): this charm lets the exalt awaken a free evocation from any artifact in his possession. It may only be used on one artifact at a time. Repurchase upgrades this charm to awaken two evocations from the same artifact.<br /> 4) You could also have a series of charms with effects that differ based on the material of certain artifacts. This could be especially useful for charms trees that don't tie nicely to artifacts that are known for evocations (for instance, <b>most </b>social interactions aren't benefited by swords and medicine doesn't really benefit from armor).<br /> 5) Another series of charms that differs based on the tags of the weapon/armor being used.<br /> <br /> <br /> I supposed one thing you could also say is that Evocations are this character's Supernal meaning that he won't be subject to essence limitations on the charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=1g_IC644YJoiVAm6ngqcBmsQtff2YYtd3pDbZpaOxx4o\" target=\"_blank\">My Exalted Character Creation Tool may be downloaded here.</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1086797-demac-s-exalted-character-creation-tool\" target=\"_blank\">The thread talking about the tool can be found here.</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1136654-exalted-seats-of-power\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted: Seats of Power is a homebrewed manse creation system.</a><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=1oaq3wk7lJKZ022SUA4iPfGzMpmBTNXlM\" target=\"_blank\">I have a rewrite of the craft system which can be downloaded here.</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1070312-i-got-my-book-it-s-super-fancy-and-i-can-t-read-the-cover/page2\" target=\"_blank\">I like the Mesoamerican look</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2346-demac","name":"Demac","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"385"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T18:53:30-07:00","id":996933,"title":"","content":"If you saw a post by me in this thread saying that I play a custom Exalt type, I don't and that was actually my girlfriend posting with my login by mistake (it's my PC and I auto-login).<br /> <br /> But yes, I let her play a non-standard Exalt type because she's got a strong idea of what she wants and is willing to adapt her ideas if there's any concerns about power level.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T20:11:58-07:00","id":996967,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/996398-anyone-make-exigents-as-playable-characters?p=996836#post996836\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well your not really making an entire splat, and it will still be the same once the Ex book comes out. Really you just need to make the charms the player will want to learn.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well yea it will be simpified when the book comes out.<br /> <br /> Until then its basically the same as making a devil Tiger set. Trying to make a charmset which accurately expresses the themes of the Godly purview he wishes to use, then making them balanced and whatnot is going to be challenging. Very challenging.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T00:41:25-07:00","id":997040,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sandact6</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/996398-anyone-make-exigents-as-playable-characters?p=996967#post996967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well yea it will be simpified when the book comes out.<br /> <br /> Until then its basically the same as making a devil Tiger set. Trying to make a charmset which accurately expresses the themes of the Godly purview he wishes to use, then making them balanced and whatnot is going to be challenging. Very challenging.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well it can be more similar to making a God as you don't have to list all the possible charms and more list the few your character wants at first, but I see what you are saying.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T08:35:02-07:00","id":997157,"title":"","content":"I don't have any players trying to play an Exigent (though one of them <i>is </i>playing a Lunar, which at this point isn't too much different), but I have drafted an Exigent antagonist for them to encounter in the future. Well...maybe I should say &quot;am in the process of drafting&quot; because it's slow going. I will say that it's really important to very clearly define the god that shaped the Exigent's Exaltation before starting in on the Exigent herself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Share your wonders in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop#post823884\" target=\"_blank\">The Artifact and Evocation Workshop</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1315-ferryman","name":"Ferryman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1315_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T08:42:25-07:00","id":997162,"title":"","content":"I really want to make an Exigent of Artificial Flight. I figured I could cobble a charm set together based on some of the Solar Craft and Thrown charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T08:42:47-07:00","id":997163,"title":"","content":"Ok. Trying this again! I play a non-canonical Exalt type in Lioness' game though my character is not an Exigent.<br /> <br /> I\u2019ve found it much easier than a Devil Tiger because I didn\u2019t have to start with an Excellency that required me to write a paragraph about my character\u2019s personality with 25-30 keywords, I just had to decide upon a dice cap and some kind of gimmick that looks appropriate/interesting.<br /> <br /> My character\u2019s not tied to a canonical NPC nor rooted in a single well-worn concept so I\u2019m not overly worried that the Exigent book is going to have the same idea as me an execute it better, but that\u2019s less likely with a concept revolving around swords unless you settle on something specific.<br /> <br /> I\u2019ve never seen Bleach or played much of the Elder Scrolls games so I'm not sure how specific a Shinigami or a Spellsword is. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>success is the ability to go from one failure to the next without any loss of enthusiasm","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1115-the-hug-ninja","name":"The Hug Ninja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1115_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"324"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T11:44:11-07:00","id":997279,"title":"","content":"Eldagusto, sounds like something you *should* be able to do with a Solar from what I know. Is he more attracted by the story hooks for an Exigent, like having a specific god? If so can you just use Solar rules and have him technically be an Exigent in game?<br /> <br /> (As an aside to this thread and the complexities of Exigents, I wonder if the Exigents book will probably try to limit some of the complexities by offering a kind of combinations of templates approach. <br /> <br /> So like if you want to play a chosen of a city god, then you pick the Architect Charm cascades (a la Revana Quin), then if your city god is, a god of a slaver city, then you can also pick up a cascade themed around oppression and liberation as well, and so on and so on.<br /> <br /> Then you can customise their strength from there by picking their highest level of sorcery access and their experience costs and their essence calculations and maximum dice pool and whether they get anything like a supernal ability, etc.<br /> <br /> I don't really have any clue though. Potentially to do anything like the above you'd need a very big book, to even just sketch out the outlines of Charmsets with lots of in between blanks to be filled in.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T12:39:27-07:00","id":997310,"title":"","content":"Yes he is probably going to be a Solar. Only one member of my group even knows what the Exalted Are so everyone is going to Exalt in game. I had everyone make characters that had the potential to be badass or already were, he is a very unibomber hermit type who lives in the woods and is the type where he would bargain for Power if the character who he has a defining tie to is threatened or Exalts and he is left behind.<br /> <br /> He is probably going to be a Solar, Night or Dawn Caste, but On my way! Keeping my options open. We are not sure how often he will play, if most games or only every other or once a month.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T12:43:52-07:00","id":997311,"title":"","content":"Also what do think about Exigents growing more powerful then their Patron Gods by far, like Strawmaiden Janeth seemed to start out stronger then her Field/Harvest God and he sacrificed himself to make her. So if she lived a few Centuries would her charms evolve her towards a more Primordial reaper harvester archtype, like Saturn?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T16:01:54-07:00","id":997416,"title":"","content":"Well...to start, there is no reason to believe that Strawmaiden Janest will necessarily live beyond her own natural lifespan. It's pretty clearly indicated that the longevity bestowed upon the canon Exalted is an engineered part of their Exaltations, <i>not </i>an inherent part of <i>all </i>Exaltations. So, there's that.<br /> <br /> But assuming for the moment that she could and did live a few centuries? Yeah, I'd be fine with her surpassing her patron. The power of the Exigence doesn't originate with the god, after all - it originates in the Fires of Exigence themselves, from which the Unconquered Sun kindles that Exaltation and passes it on to whatever god he has decided merits it for them to catalyze into a mortal. Doing so might consume a lesser deity (like Ten Sheaves), weaken or lessen them for a time, or be just the equivalent of a hard day's work depending on the might of the god involved (I would assume that it's not trivial for any deity short of the Celestial Incarnae). The potential of the Exalt so created might greatly surpass that of his or her patron, and in fact this is exactly why Ten Sheaves did what he did. He knew he couldn't stop the Fair Folk, so he was doomed in any case. But maybe Janest could do what was beyond him.<br /> <br /> And really, that's been the driving purpose behind all of the Exaltations we've ever seen, hasn't it? Mortals imbued with the power of the divine to accomplish things that their creators cannot. Because for all their power, the gods are limited in ways that mortals aren't. I would try to make that a foundation of any Exigent's origin story.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Share your wonders in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop#post823884\" target=\"_blank\">The Artifact and Evocation Workshop</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1315-ferryman","name":"Ferryman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1315_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T11:32:39-08:00","id":1003505,"title":"","content":"A major part of how I build non-canonical Exalts is that I try to apply the basic concept to Attributes or Abilities that aren't a logical fit for it.<br /> <br /> My character's primary gimmick is that she regenerates physical damage so I found Resistance the most boring ability to brainstorm ideas for because it tells us nothing new. The other trees speak of how a power like that has informed her ideology and tactics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>success is the ability to go from one failure to the next without any loss of enthusiasm","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1115-the-hug-ninja","name":"The Hug Ninja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1115_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"324"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}